  u: `<p>Logs grow at the end, so <code>tail</code> is the #1 troubleshooting tool: <code>tail -n 50 /var/log/syslog</code>, <code>tail -f app.log</code> while reproducing a bug. Combine with grep: <code>tail -f app.log | grep ERROR</code>.</p><p><code>-f</code> follows the open file descriptor; if the log is rotated (renamed and recreated), use <code>-F</code> to reopen the new file by name.</p>`,
  adv: `<p>tail seeks from the end (<code>lseek(fd, -bufsize, SEEK_END)</code>) and scans backwards for newlines, so it's O(N lines) not O(file size). For -f, GNU tail uses <code>inotify(7)</code> to sleep until IN_MODIFY, falling back to polling every second on filesystems that don't support it (some network mounts). On pipes it can't seek and must read everything.</p>`,
